# Product Requirements Document (PRD)

**Product Name:** TestForge (Working Title)

**Document Version:** 1.0.0

**Status:** Ready for Engineering Review

**Target Release:** Q3 2026

---

## 1. Executive Summary & Problem Statement

### 1.1 Executive Summary

TestForge is a white-label, multi-tenant assessment and test management SaaS platform designed for enterprise talent acquisition and higher education institutions. The platform handles end-to-end evaluation lifecycles: administrative authoring via bulk Excel ingestion, dynamic brand theming, strictly timed multi-sectional assessments (Technical, Aptitude, Behavioral), candidate pre-briefing, real-time autosaved test navigation, and pre-submission audit reviews.

### 1.2 Problem Statement

Current assessment tooling forces organizations into one of two compromises: rigid, off-the-shelf software with third-party branding and brittle question import formats, or bloated enterprise LMS systems that lack section-level timer enforcement and autosave resilience during unreliable network conditions. Organizations require a customizable assessment engine that safeguards academic and hiring integrity while offering candidates an intuitive, low-friction evaluation experience.

### 1.3 Goals & Success Metrics

| Metric Category | Target KPI | Measurement Method |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **System Reliability** | $\ge 99.99\%$ response persistence | Telemetry logging of sync events vs. total client events |
| **Operational Efficiency** | $\le 60$ seconds to ingest 500 questions via Excel | Pipeline execution logging from upload to database write |
| **Candidate Experience** | $\le 0.1\%$ support tickets regarding lost progress | Help-desk ticket categorization tagged with `assessment-drop` |
| **Test Completion Integrity** | 100% server-side timer enforcement accuracy | Discrepancy delta between client clock and server validation token |

